 <section class="wrap section editorial-pair"><figure><Photo id={27}/><figcaption>Imagined medina lane · generated illustration.</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">THE MEDINA</p><h2>Look closer.<br/><em>Walk a little further.</em></h2><p>Tetouan’s medina is inscribed on UNESCO’s World Heritage List. Its urban fabric reflects a long relationship between northern Morocco and Andalusia.</p><p>Our imagined house belongs to this setting: a courtyard retreat from which to explore the city. Its exact address is deliberately unspecified.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/837/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read about the medina at UNESCO <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
 <section class="wrap section craft-story"><div><p class="eyebrow">IN THE DETAILS</p><h2>Timber. Plaster.<br/><em>The marks of making.</em></h2><p>Take time for the texture of a door, the shadow inside a passage, the proportions of a threshold. These details inform the material language of DAR SERA.</p><p class="fine-print">Destination images on this concept site are generated illustrations. They do not document an exact street, monument, artisan or property.</p></div><figure><Photo id={28}/><figcaption>Imagined architectural detail · no historic attribution.</figcaption></figure></section>
